‹Heading1,b:Plan: a link checker›
‹Heading1,b:for the site builder›
‹Rule:────────────────────›

‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:For agentic›
‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:workers: work›
‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:through the steps›
‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:in order and tick›
‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:each box when its›
‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:tests pass.›

‹Text,b:Goal:› ‹Code: gleam check ›
reads a built site
and reports every
broken internal
link, with the page
and line it came
from.

‹Text,b:Architecture:›

  ‹Bullet:• ›A walker lists
    the pages under
    the output
    folder
  ‹Bullet:• ›A parser pulls
    every ‹Code: href › and
    ‹Code: src › out of
    each page
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›absolute URLs
      are skipped
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›fragments are
      checked
      against the
      page's own
      anchors
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›an anchor is
        any ‹Code: id ›
        attribute
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›a heading
        gets one
        from its
        text
  ‹Bullet:• ›A reporter
    prints one line
    per broken link
    and sets the
    exit code

‹Text,b:Tech stack:› Go 1.27,
‹Code: golang.org/x/net/ht›
‹Code:ml ›, the standard
library otherwise.

